                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1539-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Supercardioid" title="Supercardioid" ></span>Samson Q1U</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Supercardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Q1U is a handheld dynamic mic with onboard ADC and USB output. Samson claims this to be the first dynamic mic with a USB interface.</p><p>The mic has a frequency response of 50-16kHz, with gentle roll-off below 100Hz and broad mid rise between 2 and 10kHz.</p><p>The onboard A/D converter operates at 16-bit, up to 48kHz.</p><p>Downloadable Softpre apple for OSX and Windows provide additional features: gain, LED input metering, Low-cut filter, polarity.</p><p>Includes desktop mic stand, mic clip, USB cable and carry pouch, Cakewalk Music Creator LE software.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Samson/Q1U">Samson Q1U</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2006.</p>
